      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " The second kind of renunciation is the quitting of the weary: \"this work is painful, I will leave it.\" Osho would say: the rajasic renouncer is not a seeker; he is a tired man who has given his fatigue a holy name. He abandons the work — and the fruit of renunciation eludes him, because he has renounced the work, not the clinging. He will carry the clinging into the next work, and the next. The test is simple: if your renunciation is a relief from effort, it is rajasic. The sattvic renunciation is not a relief from effort; it is a relief from grasping — the work continues, the effort continues, only the suffering stops."]
