      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " The rajasic pleasure is the advertisement of the senses: nectar on the tongue, poison in the digestion. Osho would say: every sensual delight — the extra glass, the purchased thrill, the orgasm of acquisition — is nectar at the moment of contact and poison in its aftermath: the hangover, the emptiness, the craving for more. The rajasic pleasure is not wrong; it is simply a loan that is repaid with interest. The wise man does not become an enemy of the senses; he becomes a connoisseur of consequences. He tastes the first sip of nectar — and remembers the last taste of the poison."]
